    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "What HYDRA is", "items": [
      "A local workbench for designing languages (metamodels and grammars), modeling with them, and transforming them",
      "All your work lives on your own machine; it does not depend on a remote server",
      "You can connect external tools (Git, transformation engines) whenever you need them, never by default"
    ]},
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "How the capabilities relate", "items": [
      "The metamodel is the foundation: models, validations, grammars and events are all defined over its types",
      "An existing model is the starting point both for transforming it and for generating/publishing a result",
      "Design (or import) a metamodel or a grammar for your language",
      "Define validations to catch mistakes early",
      "Create models with that language and transform them into other formats",
      "Publish or generate a final project once it's ready"
    ]},
